From: hero-crew session — unify loop marketplace under astra namespace
Subject: chore(marketplace): unify loop under astra namespace

Brings the loop plugin's marketplace.json in line with crew's so users
install both plugins with the same `@astra` namespace:

  /plugin install crew@astra
  /plugin install loop@astra

Apply IN THE LOOP REPO session (per memory feedback_marketplace_session_constraint.md
— marketplace version/identity changes must be done in the target repo's
own session, not cross-session).

## How to apply

```bash
cd C:/work/mega/loop
# Save the patch block below to /tmp/loop-astra-namespace.patch (or similar)
git apply --check /tmp/loop-astra-namespace.patch  # dry-run
git apply /tmp/loop-astra-namespace.patch
git diff                                            # verify
git add .claude-plugin/marketplace.json
git commit -m "chore(marketplace): unify loop under astra namespace

Brings marketplace.json identity in line with crew/hero-crew so users
install both plugins via the same namespace:

  /plugin install loop@astra

Changes:
- marketplace.json 'name': 'loop' -> 'astra'
- marketplace.json 'owner.name': 'shishkosv' -> 'astra'
- description rewritten to drop the 'decoupled from astra' framing

Consumer impact: existing 'loop@loop' installs continue to work; new
installs should prefer 'loop@astra'. Document the migration in the
README pinned-release callout."

git push origin main
```

## Consumer migration

After the loop repo lands this patch + cuts a release tag, consumers do
once:

```bash
/plugin remove loop@loop      # old standalone marketplace name
/plugin install loop@astra    # unified namespace
```

The hero-crew marketplace.json does NOT need to change — it already
declares `name: astra` and only ships `crew`. The loop plugin stays in
its own repo + own marketplace.json file; only the marketplace's
identity (name + owner) is unified.

