## Rollback

```bash
cd C:/work/mega/loop
git revert HEAD
git push origin main
```

Consumers stay on `loop@astra` install; the marketplace identity reverts
to `name: "loop"` / `owner.name: "shishkosv"` and existing installs keep
working. Only NEW installs would once again need to use `loop@loop`.

## Why not edit cross-repo from this session

Memory `feedback_marketplace_session_constraint.md` captured the rule:
companion plugin version bumps in marketplace.json must be done in the
target repo's own session, not cross-session. Same rule applies to
marketplace identity changes — they're semantically version-class
metadata.

Cross-session edits would:

- bypass the loop repo's CI gates on the change
- skip the loop repo's CHANGELOG entry (consumers won't see the
  migration callout)
- risk drift if the loop repo has any in-flight branch touching the
  same file
